# The browser extension is built and published separately, never deployed.
# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored "extension/" also matches
# src/lib/extension/, which pruned the extension API's shared library from the
# deployment and failed the production build.
#
# `/extension/*` rather than `/extension/`, so the negation below can take: an
# ignored *directory* is never descended into, and a `!` rule on something
# inside it has no effect.
/extension/*

# ...except its TypeScript source, which has to exist for the production build
# to typecheck. `next build` typechecks everything in the root tsconfig program,
# which includes `scripts/**`, and `scripts/smoke-contact-profile-format.ts`
# imports the extension's pure DOM readers to exercise them headlessly. Without
# these files the build fails with "Cannot find module
# '../extension/src/inject/adapters/linkedin-profile'" — a failure that appears
# ONLY on Vercel, because a local checkout and CI both have the whole tree.
#
# Nothing in the app imports these, so they are typechecked and never bundled.
!/extension/src/
